      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "To gain a better way of thinking about medical technology and our human mortality, we should begin backward. Death should be seen as the necessary and inevitable end point of medical care.... We as a society remain uncertain about the status of patients who manage to combine, in a bewildering way, elements of both life and death."},
